questions.question:
A body of mass 2 kg moves along the +x axis at 5 m/s. From t = 0, a force along the x-axis acts on it as follows:
- the force is +6 N from t = 0 to t = 2 s;
- it then decreases linearly to −6 N at t = 4 s, passing through zero at t = 3 s;
- it stays at −6 N from t = 4 s to t = 6 s.
What is the velocity of the body at t = 6 s?
